WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:06.339
There are situations in programming where
one wants to raise specific types of errors

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:11.600
given a specific situation for an error, such
as for dividing by zero or when a value out

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.180
of range is entered when getting input from
someone.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:20.510
For those situations, the raise keyword raises
either a type of error supported in Python

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.200
or a custom error.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.240
Let’s look at a simple code example for
asking for input for the Fahrenheit temperature

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:33.710
for absolute zero, which is -459.67 degrees
Fahrenheit.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:38.010
That code is in this 525-raise file.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.379
To focus on the raise error, this code does
not run through guesses until the person guesses

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:43.640
correctly.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:51.770
But, if the person tries to enter a positive
number in the input statement on line 1, which

00:00:51.770 --> 00:01:00.030
converts the input to a floating decimal,
the raise statement on line 3 runs.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:11.409
The raise statement raises a value error,
one of many built-in error types in Python.

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:14.630
Why raise an error rather than correct the
player?

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:21.439
If game activity is being logged, and this
app is being tested, one may be writing results

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:27.439
to a log, and raising errors is one way to
spot unwanted responses within an app and

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:30.040
then address fixes for those responses.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:39.470
I will run the code and enter a positive number
on purpose.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.860
Sure enough, the error is raised.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:59.579
If I rerun the code and enter a negative result,
I get the print statement from line 5.

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:05.630
Again, raising errors allows a developer to
control the type of error to raise and log

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:07.140
the error if necessary.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.530
